<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Irineu Evangelista de Sousa, Viscount of Mauá</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1813–1889</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Viscount of Mauá, Baron of Mauá</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Irineu Evangelista de Sousa, Viscount of Mauá, was a Brazilian industrialist, banker and entrepreneur. He built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>'s first railway, opened near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a> in 1854, and invested in shipyards, gas lighting, steamship lines and banks in Brazil, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>. His business empire collapsed in the 1870s, but he is remembered as a pioneer of industrialisation in a slave-based agrarian economy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/irineu-evangelista-de-sousa-viscount-of-maua.jpg" alt="Irineu Evangelista de Sousa, Viscount of Mauá" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maua_00.JPG: Joaquim Insley Pacheco (1830-1912) derivative work: Kingpin13 (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maua_00.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
